From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:47:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 54/56] LibWeb: IdleDeadline.timeRemaining() puts the deadline
 on the global's clock

computeDeadline answers on the shared clock and now is relative to the time origin, so timeRemaining() was the time origin plus up to 50 ms.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/RequestIdleCallback/IdleDeadline.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/RequestIdleCallback/IdleDeadline.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/RequestIdleCallback/IdleDeadline.cpp
index de4614a29f..f6f37f9664 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/RequestIdleCallback/IdleDeadline.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/RequestIdleCallback/IdleDeadline.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,10 @@ double IdleDeadline::time_remaining() const
     // 1. Let now be a DOMHighResTimeStamp representing current high resolution time in milliseconds.
     auto now = HighResolutionTime::current_high_resolution_time(HTML::current_global_object());
     // 2. Let deadline be the result of calling IdleDeadline's get deadline time algorithm.
-    auto deadline = event_loop.compute_deadline();
+    // NB: computeDeadline answers on the shared clock (the last idle period's start is the unsafe shared current time) and now is
+    //     relative to the global's time origin: put the deadline on now's clock, or timeRemaining() is the time origin plus up
+    //     to 50 ms (Chrome never answers more than 50).
+    auto deadline = HighResolutionTime::relative_high_resolution_time(event_loop.compute_deadline(), HTML::current_global_object());
     // 3. Let timeRemaining be deadline - now.
     auto time_remaining = deadline - now;
     // 4. If timeRemaining is negative, set it to 0.
